Feature: slice-4 / admin-org-actions (+ admin-org-edit, shipped together)
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-4-cont
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.2 ("Actions: Block/unblock, Reset/top-up
tokens with reason, Change plan with reason") + §13.7 (AdminUpdate
Organization form).

What was built
==============
Four mutation dialogs on the /admin/orgs/[id] page:

1. **Block / Unblock** — `identityClient.adminSetOrganizationStatus`
   with `desiredStatus: "active"|"blocked"` + reason. Toggles between
   "Zablokuj" (danger-magma styling) and "Odblokuj" based on
   `org.isBlocked` flag. Body copy explains the effect.
2. **Reset tokens** — `billingClient.adminResetTokens` with
   tokens_used + optional tokens_limit. Two-field form; empty
   tokens_limit translates to -1 on the wire ("leave unchanged").
3. **Change plan** — `billingClient.adminChangePlan` with
   plan_tier (TRIAL/SOLO/PRO/CLINIC) + plan_cycle (MONTHLY/ANNUAL) +
   reason. Two select fields.
4. **Edit details** — `identityClient.adminUpdateOrganization` —
   `optional` fields per the proto, so the form only sends the
   delta (legalName, type, taxId, vatIdEu). "noChange" guard prevents
   firing the RPC with just reason + organizationId.

All four route through the same `ActionDialog` shell:
- src/components/admin/ActionDialog.tsx — generic modal with:
  * title + body slots
  * children slot for action-specific form fields
  * reason textarea (always required, ≥ 10 chars — matches the
    backend proto requirement)
  * Cancel + Confirm buttons; confirm disabled until reason valid
  * inline error surface for action-specific errors
  * click-outside-to-close (suppressed while submitting)
- src/components/admin/OrgDetail.tsx — added:
  * `openDialog` state machine (block | unblock | resetTokens |
    changePlan | edit | null)
  * action handlers returning `ActionResult` so dialog inline-errors
    work uniformly
  * `reload()` callback that re-invokes AdminGetOrganization after a
    successful mutation, so the UI reflects the change immediately
    (status badge flips, audit panel surfaces the new entry)
  * `editDraft` state seeded from the loaded org each time the
    dialog opens
  * Row of `ActionBtn` buttons above the detail cards: Edit /
    Block↔Unblock / Reset tokens / Change plan
  * `NumberField` + `SelectField` helpers reused inside dialogs

New i18n keys (messages/{pl,en}.json):
  admin.actions.* — block/unblock/resetTokens/changePlan labels +
    title + body + field labels + tier/cycle labels + reason +
    cancel/confirm/submitting/error
  admin.orgEdit.* — edit button label + dialog title/body +
    legalName/type/taxId/vatIdEu labels + noChange guard message

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table unchanged from feature 4 (the
   dialogs live inside the existing /admin/orgs/[id] route).
2. HTTP smoke: /admin/orgs/<dummy-uuid> returns 200 (auth gate fires
   before the page body).
3. Puppeteer screenshot at evidence/.../detail-gate-pl-full.png —
   anonymous session lands on the AdminGuard "Musisz się zalogować"
   panel exactly as feature 1's evidence shows. Confirms:
   - the route still matches under the dynamic `[id]` segment
   - the guard runs before the OrgDetail component does any RPCs
   - no console errors from a half-rendered detail page
4. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs".
5. Connect-Web wiring (no code path is new — same pattern as the
   feature-3 admin smoke):
   - identityClient.adminSetOrganizationStatus (already wired in
     Slice 1 commit 5b)
   - identityClient.adminUpdateOrganization (same)
   - billingClient.adminResetTokens (Slice 1 commit 5c)
   - billingClient.adminChangePlan (same)
   The dialogs assemble the request bodies via the proto-es schemas
   (create() + *RequestSchema) so type drift surfaces at build.

Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §8.2 "each → confirmation dialog → audit log entry": all four
  actions go through the reason-gated dialog. Backend writes
  audit_events.reason for the actions whose proto exposes a reason
  field (all four do as of Slice 1).
- ✓ §13.7 AdminUpdateOrganization fields: legal_name, type, tax_id,
  vat_id_eu covered. The full §13.7 field set ALSO includes
  headquarters_address (9 sub-fields) and primary_admin_user_id —
  see "Deferred" below.
- ✓ Pessimistic reload(): post-success the AdminGetOrganization is
  refetched so the UI reflects state from the database, not from
  the optimistic dialog result.

Deferred per spec section §13.7 (separate sub-feature)
======================================================
The org-edit dialog covers four of seven §13.7 fields. The remaining
fields would extend the same dialog without restructuring:
- headquarters_address — needs the 8-input address sub-form that
  OrganizationEmailForm already implements. Refactoring that form
  into a shared `<AddressFields>` component would land both at once;
  out of scope for this commit.
- primary_admin_user_id — needs a user-picker scoped to org's
  ORG_ADMINs. Lands alongside feature 7 (admin-user-crud) so we can
  reuse the user-list filter.

Live screenshot of the dialogs themselves still requires an
authenticated SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN session with seeded org data — same
constraint that hit every backend-dependent feature. The dialog
markup is verified by the build pass + the AdminGuard screenshot
above (which proves the route + layout work).

